Architectural decision ticket arising from the git-bug competitive teardown
(session 2026-10-02). Today ticgit stores the *current state* of each ticket
directly under `ticgit:tickets:<uuid>:<field>` and syncs those keys, so two
clones editing the same ticket concurrently collide at merge with last-write-wins
(LWW) clobber.

Proposal: make an **append-only operation log** the conflict-free source of truth
— the only thing that syncs and merges — and repurpose the current state keys as
a **disposable, rebuildable derived cache** so `ti list` / `ti show` stay fast
without replaying the log on every command.

This mirrors git-bug's own design (operation DAG as truth + separate rebuildable
cache). It unlocks free history/blame/point-in-time queries and removes LWW
clobber, at the cost of a replay+cache layer and a format migration.

Scope of THIS ticket = make the architectural decision concrete and durable
(spec attached). Implementation is sequenced in sub-issues/follow-ups per the
teardown roadmap; this is not a single-PR change.

